# Project rules / knowledge

## What this is
- solar-ctl: RPi-based controller for a **Deye inverter** (modbus), publishing to
  Home Assistant energy. Display: 2.79" NV3007 TFT.
- `fw/` — Yocto **kas** firmware build (this is the active part).
- `inv_ctl/` — the inverter-controller app (C++23, glibmm main loop + LVGL
  9.4): SDL2 on laptop, fbdev on target; built into the image as the
  `inv-ctl` recipe (`fw/recipes-apps/inv-ctl/`), started via
  `inv-ctl.service`. See `inv_ctl/README.md`.
- Target board: **Raspberry Pi Zero W** (`machine: raspberrypi0-wifi`).

## Firmware build (fw/)
- Build with `kas build fw/kas-rpi0.yml` from the repo root (tested with kas 5.5).
- Release: Yocto **wrynose**. No poky: standalone oe-core + our distro conf
  `fw/conf/distro/solar-ctl.conf` (`TCLIBC=musl`, `INIT_MANAGER=systemd`,
  trimmed `DISTRO_FEATURES_DEFAULTS`).
- Layer refs: **LOCKED since 2026-09-29 (v0.1.0 prep)** — `fw/kas-rpi0.lock.yml`
  is committed and pins the exact bench-validated generation: oe-core
  `883075157987ca300af59185b903d6d1977234c3`, bitbake
  `f0df79b6b56f6a69067adf974978d9405077f246`, meta-raspberrypi
  `f62c67921474370829d24a4fa01ef88543f3906b`, meta-oe
  `14282a02be9c74a1276a7cda7d6c89e054699a11`, meta-swupdate
  `c0658455606b3a37d85d7cf03703d8b8d2ead667`. kas auto-applies the lockfile
  to every build including the CI `fw/kas-rpi0.yml:.kas-wifi-ci.yml`
  fragment form (verified in kas 5.5 `includehandler.py`: the lock injects
  after its parent config; the url-less `solar-ctl` repo is deliberately
  NOT locked — local tree builds keep working). Bump = delete lockfile,
  `git -C layers/<repo> fetch`, `kas lock fw/kas-rpi0.yml`; float again =
  delete the lockfile. (Branch mode before this silently moved oe-core
  `88307515…→cc4695f6…` and invalidated ~50% of the CI sstate — the
  measured cause of "cache doesn't work". Old `fw/kas-baseline.yml` manual
  copy stays removed.) **Releases are automatic: push a `v*` tag** — the
  firmware workflow builds it and publishes the GitHub Release with dist/*
  (softprops action; `permissions: contents: write` already set).
- Use **GitHub mirrors**; `git.yoctoproject.org` is unreachable here (Cloudflare 403):
  use `github.com/openembedded/openembedded-core`, `openembedded/bitbake`,
  `agherzan/meta-raspberrypi`.
- The `solar-ctl` repo entry in the kas file deliberately has **no `url`**: kas
  builds from the working tree, don't "fix" it by adding a url.
- `layers/`, `build/`, `kas-build.log` are generated by kas — gitignored, never edit.
- CI cache (firmware.yml): sstate only (`build/sstate-cache`, ~1.3 GB) with a
  `yocto-*` restore-keys fallback and `-<sha>` save suffix. **Same-repo PR
  runs save too** (fixed 2026-09-29: PRs never saved, so every PR push
  restored the same stale cache — full 1h20m rebuilds even for docs-only
  changes; fork PRs still excluded). The exact restore key carries
  `github.sha` and therefore never hits on a fresh commit — all real hits
  come from the `yocto-*` fallback (by design). Do NOT cache
  `build/downloads` (~9.5 GB, 8.4 GB of it `git2` clones): GitHub's cache
  quota is 10 GB/repo and the old downloads+sstate entry sat at 9.97 GiB —
  one kernel bump from silently failing to save. `fw/kas-ci.yml` was deleted
  2026-09: its `INHERIT:remove = "rm_work"` was based on confusing rm_work
  with rm_work_and_downloads — rm_work never touches downloads/sstate, so
  it did nothing for the cache, only kept tmp/work on the runner.
- `SOLAR_WIFI_SSID/PSK/COUNTRY` are declared in `fw/kas-rpi0.yml`
  (`env:` section, CHANGEME placeholders — kas exports them to bitbake via
  BB_ENV_PASSTHROUGH_ADDITIONS and OS env vars override them). The real
  values live ONLY in the gitignored `.zed/tasks.json` "Build FW" env block
  (`.zed` is in .gitignore — keep it that way while it holds the PSK) and are
  baked into the image as a root-only 0600 file — treat built images as
  secret and never publish them. **Never put real WiFi credentials in
  committed files**; a gitignored `.kas-wifi-local.yml` fragment
  (`kas build fw/kas-rpi0.yml:.kas-wifi-local.yml`) works too — its
  local.conf `=` assignments beat the environment. CI injects them from
  Actions secrets (`SOLAR_WIFI_*`) via a generated `.kas-wifi-ci.yml`
  fragment (gitignored). Repo is PUBLIC: only bake a lab/guest SSID, never
  the real home PSK, into CI artifacts/releases. CI has a guard step that
  fails the build if any of these secret-bearing files ever get tracked by
  git (firmware.yml "Guard against committed secret files").
- `SOLAR_TZ` (kas `env:`, declared 2026-10-05) is the watch timezone:
  the `inv-ctl` recipe writes `TZ=<value>` to `/etc/default/inv-ctl`,
  which `inv-ctl.service` reads via `EnvironmentFile=-` (same
  `/etc/default` convention as dropbear). Unset = no file = UTC fallback
  (all CI builds). **musl has no zoneinfo** — value must be a POSIX TZ
  string (`CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3` = Copenhagen); a zoneinfo name is
  silently ignored by musl (= still UTC), so do_install bb-fatals on
  `:*` (glibc file form), digit-less `*/*` (names never contain the
  offset digits that every POSIX spec has), and `Etc/*` (the digit-
  carrying name exception). `create_now_local()` honours TZ via
  localtime_r — zero app code changed. Not a secret; safe in CI env.
  `/etc/default/inv-ctl` is squashfs-baked: changing TZ = rebuild+OTA.
- `SOLAR_SSH_PUBLIC_KEY` (kas `env:`, declared 2026-10-02) is baked into
  `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` by `solar-rootkeys` (python do_install;
  one public key per line, real or literal `\n` separated, OR an ABSOLUTE
  host path — same resolver convention as `solar_swu_get_key` in
  solar-swu-signing.bbclass; helper `solar_ssh_get_keys`); unset =
  bb.warn and **no authorized_keys baked** — user policy 2026-10-02:
  **no keys in the repo at all, no key = no SSH access** (the old
  committed `root_authorized_keys` sk-key fallback is deleted; CI builds
  ship keyless images; serial console stays). Value is
  key CONTENT or an absolute path — never `$HOME/...`: Zed task env does
  NOT shell-expand, and the recipe rejects it loudly rather than
  compensating for the Zed bug (use /home/... or fix tasks.json/Zed).
  Public
  half only — safe in any env/secret store, unlike WiFi/swu secrets.
  `.zed/env-inject.py`'s regex must list the var
  (`SOLAR_(WIFI|SWU|SSH)_...`) or tasks.json silently ignores it.
  `do_install[vardeps]` pins it (read by NAME inside python = invisible
  to vartable hashing — the do_swu_signing_keys stale-task trap again).
  **/root is on the read-only squashfs: authorized_keys is
  rebuild-only — it cannot be appended on a running target.**

## Yocto/wrynose recipe gotchas (learned the hard way)
- `S = "${WORKDIR}"` is rejected on wrynose — use `S = "${UNPACKDIR}"` and
  `${UNPACKDIR}/<file>` paths for `file://` SRC_URI files.
- A line whose first char is `}` inside a recipe shell/python function breaks
  bitbake's parser (e.g. a `network={...}` heredoc). Use template files + sed.
- **Bare `$VAR` in a shell recipe function is NOT expanded by bitbake and
  NOT exported to the task env** — it silently reads empty. Only the
  braced `${VAR}` form triggers bitbake's textual expansion + dependency
  tracking (hit 2026-10-05: SOLAR_TZ was present in the datastore per
  `bitbake -e`, yet `[ -n "$SOLAR_TZ" ]` was false and the
  /etc/default/inv-ctl bake skipped without a word; `${SOLAR_TZ}` fixed
  it). Python functions differ: there `d.getVar("VAR")` is the mechanism
  (and needs vardeps, see solar-rootkeys).
- **A dangling `.bbappend` is a hard ERROR on wrynose, not a warning**: any
  `*.bbappend` in an *active* layer must match a recipe that is also visible.
  Adding `swupdate_%.bbappend` to `fw/` killed the image build (PR #1) with
  `ERROR: No recipes in default available for: .../swupdate_%.bbappend`, even
  though nothing in the image references swupdate. Every layer is parsed by
  every build. Fix = put such recipes in a layer that only the kas config
  needing them adds (a separate layer), not in `fw/`. (This was the whole
  point of the old `fw-swupdate/` gate layer — retired 2026-09-28 now that
  `fw/kas-rpi0.yml` itself adds meta-swupdate.)
- In kas, `repos.<id>.layers` is a **mapping** (layer path -> null | disabled
  | {prio}), so an including config that adds a key ADDS a layer while the rest
  of the parent entry survives; `target:` on the other hand is a list and gets
  REPLACED wholesale.
- `serial-console` is **not** a valid IMAGE_FEATURE on wrynose (it silently
  skips the image recipe). With systemd the serial getty comes automatically
  from `ENABLE_UART=1` + `SERIAL_CONSOLES` (systemd-serialgetty).
- musl + systemd builds fine but bitbake warns it is *experimental* upstream.
- meta-raspberrypi adds `kernel-modules` (= all ~1800 modules) and BT firmware
  to `MACHINE_EXTRA_RRECOMMENDS` on every rpi image; `solar-ctl-image.bb`
  removes them. When a kernel feature is needed, add the specific
  `kernel-module-*` package instead of re-enabling `kernel-modules`.
- `ENABLE_USB_ETH` does not exist; USB gadget mode is `ENABLE_DWC2_PERIPHERAL = "1"`.
- Keep the image minimal: base is `core-image-minimal` + targeted adds only;
  don't pull `packagegroup-core-basic`/`-full-cmdline` style groups.
- WiFi creds (see the build section above for the full policy): locally they
  come from the Zed task env / OS environment. kas only passes env vars that
  are DECLARED in the kas config `env:` section through to bitbake
  (BB_ENV_PASSTHROUGH_ADDITIONS) — arbitrary undeclared env vars are ignored
  (that was the trap with the original tasks.json env block before the
  `env:` section existed). CI uses the generated fragment instead.
- **Never use `rm_work_and_downloads`** (use plain `INHERIT += "rm_work"`):
  it puts DL_DIR under `tmp/work/<machine>/<PN>/downloads` and deletes it in
  do_rm_work — breaks recipes built target+native from one tarball (git,
  gettext: `tar: Cannot open` in do_unpack). Its leftover do_fetch sstate
  objects keep stale paths and poison the cache even after reverting; wipe
  `build/tmp` + `build/sstate-cache` if recovering.
- Licenses: `LICENSE_FLAGS_ACCEPTED = "synaptics-killswitch"` is required by
  linux-firmware-rpidistro; keep it set.

## Kernel / device-tree (learned 2026-09, display + RS485 work)
- Kernel trim: `DISABLE_VC4GRAPHICS = "1"` (kas local_conf_header) drops the
  vc4graphics machine feature, else meta-raspberrypi's `vc4graphics.cfg`
  re-enables DRM_VC4 on top of our fragment. Our fragment:
  `fw/recipes-kernel/linux/files/solar-ctl-slim.cfg` (kernel-yocto applies
  `file://*.cfg` from SRC_URI automatically; linux-raspberrypi DOES require
  linux-yocto.inc). Keep `CONFIG_DRM=y`+`DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION=y`+`DRM_PANEL_MIPI_DBI`.
  **`# CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE is not set`** (added 2026-10-02): fbcon
  otherwise binds the VT to /dev/fb0 and prints boot text + login prompt
  onto the TFT beside the LVGL UI. `DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION` does NOT select
  it, so /dev/fb0 survives for inv-ctl; kernel text stays on the
  mini-UART console. Makes the manual
  `echo 0 > /sys/class/vtconsole/vtcon1/bind` hack unnecessary.
- Custom DTBOs: drop `.dts` in `fw/recipes-kernel/linux/files/`, copy to
  `${S}/arch/arm/boot/dts/overlays/` in `do_configure:append` (bbappend),
  append to `RPI_KERNEL_DEVICETREE_OVERLAYS` **in kas local_conf_header**
  (not the bbappend — IMAGE_BOOT_FILES is evaluated in the image recipe,
  which never sees kernel-recipe appends). The overlay MUST also be
  registered in `arch/arm/boot/dts/overlays/Makefile`'s `dtbo-y` list
  (we do it via `0001-overlays-register-…patch`): kbuild gives "No rule
  to make target" for unregistered overlays even as explicit make
  targets. kbuild maps `x.dtbo` ← `x-overlay.dts` (scripts/Makefile.dtbs),
  so `nv3007-overlay.dts` registers as **`nv3007.dtbo`** (no `-overlay`
  suffix) — and kernel-yocto COMMITS SRC_URI patches onto the shared
  kernel-source branch: if a patch changes, `git reset --hard
  <SRCREV>` in work-shared kernel-source before rebuilding, or the old
  commit lingers. Validate offline with the built kernel's
  `scripts/dtc/dtc` + `gcc -E -nostdinc -I <kernel-source>/include -x
  assembler-with-cpp` (dtc alone fails on `#include <dt-bindings/...>`).
- NV3007 TFT (corrected 2026-09): the panel is a **2.79" TZT 142×428
  portrait** module, not a 240×320 ILI9341 — use the generic
  `panel-mipi-dbi` driver (`compatible = "panel-mipi-dbi-spi"`;
  `CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_MIPI_DBI=m` already in bcmrpi_defconfig). Mode comes
  from a `panel-timing` child node in the overlay; binding reality
  (bench-verified 2026-10-02, kernel 6.18): `width-mm`/`height-mm` are
  REQUIRED (missing → probe -EINVAL; 0/0 = "unknown size" is legal) and
  EVERY timing prop must be 0 EXCEPT hactive/vactive and the back-porches
  — nonzero hsync/vsync lens or front porches → "panel-timing out of
  bounds", probe -EINVAL. The back-porches double as the GRAM x/y offset
  of the visible window: this TZT module needs `hback-porch = <14>`
  (GRAM kx=14, else a stale-pixel column band; ky=0 — ruler pattern
  flush both ends). A speckled white line on one long edge of this TZT
  module is **not** software — full exoneration bench 2026-10-05:
  fb edge columns uniformly dark; widening the DT window (13/144, then
  11/148) no effect; stripes painted into fb cols outside the window
  invisible on glass (displayed set == calibrated window); SPI 2 MHz vs
  16 MHz no effect; external clean 3V3 no effect (not the Pi rail);
  MADCTL MX flip (live-patched bin via bind-mount + spi rebind) leaves
  leaves it glued to the same physical edge; SOUCTRL column windows E0h-F2h
  (§6.6.1, per-column precharge/discharge ranges) widened to chip reset
  defaults no effect; **three separate modules show it identically**; and the
  vendor-published NV3007A SPI init for this exact glass
  (`fw/docs/nv3007a-ivo-spi-init.txt`, OSPtek repo
  `osptek/tft-2.79-142x428-spi-nv3007`, CC BY 4.0) diffs **byte-for-byte
  identical to our 120-command shipped blob** — the init sequence is exonerated
  by identity, not by inference (only delta: a Delay(200) after DISPON).
  Verdict: source-driver/COF bonding artifact of the TZT product line —
  mitigate by bezel or another module family, do not re-litigate in
  software. On-device `fbdump` (repo-root `fbdump/`, recipe `solar-fbdump`,
  in the image) is the screenshot tool: /dev/fb0 → PNG to file or stdout
  (`ssh board fbdump > shot.png`; `-b` for base64 when bytes must cross an
  interactive pty — raw binary through one is silently mangled). Zero deps
  (hand-rolled PNG + zlib stored blocks); device defaults baked via CMake
  `FBDUMP_*` (fb dev, fallback geometry), CLI `-d/-g/-o` overrides.
  `fw/tools/fb-dump.sh` wraps it host-side (thin ssh wrapper; errors
  cleanly on images predating the tool). Unit tests (added 2026-10-06):
  Catch2 v3.7.1 amalgamated (same pin as inv_ctl), `FBDUMP_BUILD_TESTS`
  default OFF (Yocto never FetchContents), CI `fbdump` job in firmware.yml.
  `tests/test_png.cpp` #includes `src/main.cpp` (`FBDUMP_TESTS_BUILD` compiles
  its `main()` out) — vectors for crc32/adler32/base64/RFC + 76-col wrap +
  565-rescale, and `tests/golden_4x4.png` (byte-exact anchor generated by the
  tool itself from `gradient_4x4.raw`; a second test validates the golden
  independently so the anchor itself cannot rot). Catch2 gotcha: `CHECK(a == b
  && c == d)` is a COMPILE error (chained-comparison guard) — split or parens.
  The controller init sequence is a **firmware file**
  `/lib/firmware/panel-mipi-dbi-spi.bin` (= compatible[0] + ".bin";
  request_firmware, retried ~every 60s) — shipped by `solar-panel-fw`
  and bench-verified lighting the glass 2026-10-02; never fabricate
  NV3007 register values. mipi-dbi has no
  DT `rotation`; rotate in software. `TINYDRM_ILI9341` is now disabled
  in the slim fragment. Modules: kernel-module-{panel-mipi-dbi,spi-bcm2835,gpio-backlight}.
- Zero W UART reality (corrected 2026-09): rpi DT names `uart0`=PL011
  (ttyAMA0), `uart1`=mini (ttyS0). On Zero W the PL011's default pads
  GPIO30–33 are wired to the onboard BCM43430 (NOT the header); the
  40-pin header's only UART pair is GPIO14/15, which **both** UARTs can
  reach — so console and native RS485 are mutually exclusive there.
  Default = mini console on 14/15; `solar-rs485` overlay moves PL011 to
  14/15 + RTS on GPIO17 (cts**rts**_gpio16 group = CTS16/RTS17, ALT3)
  and disables uart1. amba-pl011 has real RS485 support; PL011 is =y in
  bcmrpi_defconfig (no module pkg needed). `uart1` overlay ≠ PL011!
- RS485 direction: `rs485ctl` recipe (fw/recipes-support/rs485ctl) wraps
  TIOCSRS485 (enable/invert/delays) — busybox has no applet for this.
- Module pkg names are derived from the module .o name: gpio_backlight.c
  → package `kernel-module-gpio-backlight` (hyphens, not underscores);
  verify in `build/tmp/pkgdata/*/runtime/` (survives rm_work).
- `build/tmp/work-shared/raspberrypi0-wifi/kernel-source` survives rm_work
  — grep defconfigs/board DTS/overlays there instead of unpacking anything.

## A/B OTA / SWUpdate (IMPLEMENTED in-tree — full record in fw/docs/swupdate-ota.md; current-state summary in fw/docs/ab-boot-uboot.md)
- Target: A/B **squashfs-xz** read-only roots + `/etc` overlay + ext4 `/data`;
  slot switch via **U-Boot env `slot=a|b`** (plan of record since 2026-09-25,
  bench test 5 PASS). Milestone image validated on bench; signed OTA flow
  implemented 2026-09-28 and **bench-verified 2026-09-28** (URL install +
  auto-reboot B→A, `-n` + manual reboot A→B; results in
  `fw/docs/bench-2026-09-24.md` "OTA update flow verified").
- **Gate retired** (2026-09-28): `fw/kas-swupdate.yml`, the `fw-swupdate`
  layer and the parallel CI `swupdate` job are deleted. The bbappend + kconfig
  fragment now live in `fw/recipes-support/swupdate/` and are only legal there
  because `fw/kas-rpi0.yml` adds the meta-swupdate repo (dangling-bbappend
  gotcha). swupdate IS in `IMAGE_INSTALL` (on-demand CLI; its auto-enabled
  `.service`/`.socket` are deleted by an image postprocess fn).
  Merged-kconfig asserts (SIGNED_IMAGES/SIGALG_RAWRSA/HASH_VERIFY=y and —
  since the 2026-09-28 bootloader flip below — UBOOT/BOOTLOADER_DEFAULT_UBOOT/
  DOWNLOAD/DOWNLOAD_SSL=y; MTD/WEBSERVER/LUA/SCRIPTS/SURICATTA not =y) moved
  into the main firmware CI job, reading the `${T}/swupdate-merged-dotconfig`
  snapshot the bbappend still writes (`rm_work` never deletes `temp`).
  **Warm-cache trap (hit 2026-10-02, runs 36853440890/37002108982):** when
  swupdate's `do_configure` comes from sstate it is a setscene task — no
  workdir/temp is created at all, so the snapshot legitimately doesn't exist
  and the assert failed on a PR that touched nothing swupdate-related. The
  CI step now falls back to `kas shell -c "bitbake swupdate -c configure -f"`
  before asserting: a kconfig check must not depend on cache temperature.
- **Signing: RSA-4096, PKCS#1 v1.5, SHA-256 — ed25519 is impossible**
  (verified against swupdate 2026.05.1 sources + U-Boot FIT: SWUpdate streams
  `EVP_DigestVerifyUpdate/Final`, OpenSSL ed25519 is one-shot only, `openssl
  dgst -sign` refuses ed25519, FIT has no ed25519; same keypair is planned to
  sign FIT images later, which settles it). Keys env-style like WiFi:
  `SOLAR_SWU_PRIVATE_KEY` = PEM **content** or **absolute host path**
  (declared in kas `env:`) is REQUIRED — empty ⇒ hard bb.fatal; the repo
  ships NO fallback keypair (committed dev pair removed 2026-09-28: never
  let a build silently sign with a key that merely lives in the tree).
  `SOLAR_SWU_PUBLIC_KEY` optional: derived via `openssl rsa -pubout`
  (openssl-native depends added in the class) and cross-checked against the
  private key when also supplied (mismatch = fatal). CI: ONE secret
  `SOLAR_SWU_PRIVATE_KEY` + an explicit `Require signing key secret` step
  (fork PRs without secrets fail by design). Real keys:
  `fw/tools/swu-keygen.sh` → `.zed/tasks.json` env / Actions
  secret `SOLAR_SWU_PRIVATE_KEY`. Plumbing: `fw/classes/solar-swu-signing.bbclass`
  (writes `${WORKDIR}/swu-signing/{private,public}.pem` in a task wired via
  `bb.build.addtask` inside anon-python — plain `addtask ... before
  do_swuimage` breaks recipes lacking that task, and setting a `before`
  *flag* by hand does nothing; `do_swuimage[vardeps]`/`do_install[vardeps]`
  so key rotation re-runs tasks — and since the staged pub key is DERIVED,
  `do_install[vardeps]` must include `SOLAR_SWU_PRIVATE_KEY`, not just the
  public one). **vardeps must also be on
  `do_swu_signing_keys` itself** (hit 2026-09-28 when first real keys went
  into `.zed/tasks.json`): that task reads the vars via a string-literal
  variable NAME (`solar_swu_get_key(d, "SOLAR_SWU_...")`), invisible to
  vartable analysis, so without its own vardeps it replays STALE staged PEMs
  while `do_swuimage` (vardeps on the var) re-runs and silently re-signs
  with the old keypair → dev-signed `.swu` vs real-key image, `openssl
  dgst` verification failure; the tell is the staged
  `solar-ctl-swu/1.0/swu-signing/*.pem` mtimes lagging the build. Debug
  recipe (hashes only, never print PEMs): sha256 the key baked in the
  `solar-swu-agent` RPM (`./etc/solar/swupdate.pub.pem`), the
  `swu-keys/public.pem`, and `.zed/tasks.json` values (JSON-escaped `\n`
  must be unescaped; `$ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT` must be expanded — Zed does this
  itself, `.zed/env-inject.py` does it for terminal builds).
- **Single .swu, two sets** (`fw/recipes-core/images/solar-ctl-swu.bb` +
  `files/sw-description`): `stable = { main = p2 + /data/cores/slot-a/uImage;
  alt = p3 + slot-b }`, chosen at install: `swupdate -i f.swu -e
  stable,main|alt -k /etc/solar/swupdate.pub.pem`. `/usr/bin/solar-update`
  (recipe `solar-swu-agent`) ONLY derives the set from `root=` in
  /proc/cmdline, mkdirs `/data/cores/slot-{a,b}` and forwards args to
  swupdate — both `-i f.swu` and
  `-d "-u https://..."` work (CONFIG_DOWNLOAD+DOWNLOAD_SSL now on; curl+TLS
  in the image, nothing listens); `-n|--no-reboot` only plants the one-shot
  `/run/solar-update/no-reboot`. The reboot is done by **our
  solar-swupdate-progress.service** (same recipe, `swupdate-progress` now in
  the image): watches the progress socket, logs to journald, on SUCCESS runs
  `/usr/libexec/solar-swu-reboot` (consumes the marker and stays up, else
  `exec systemctl reboot` — never raw reboot(2)). Verified in 2026.05.1:
  **swupdate itself never reboots** — sw-description `reboot = true` only
  feeds progress/suricatta notifications; the progress server starts on EVERY
  run (core/swupdate.c:1116 — watcher fires for CLI -i/-d too); `-w` blocks
  silently until the socket exists; `-r` takes the NEXT WORD as its script
  (run via system()); socket path follows $RUNTIME_DIRECTORY so the unit must
  NOT set RuntimeDirectory= (both land on /tmp/swupdateprog); no CLI flag
  suppresses reboot (-R = no-reinstall) — hence the /run marker. Upstream
  swupdate-progress.service (in ${PN}-progress) stays inert (WantedBy=
  swupdate.service, deleted) and would raw-reboot; our own unit wraps the
  same binary. The
  `reboot = true` declaration stays in the signed description (stage-3
  SURICATTA consults it). The ARM is a per-set `bootenv = {name=
  "slot"; value="a|b"}` entry in sw-description: the parser resolves `bootenv`
  through the SAME set-path search as `images`, and the U-Boot backend flushes
  it via libubootenv (/etc/fw_env.config, same target as fw_setenv) ONLY after
  every image of the set installed (core/installer.c); env-write failure fails
  the update. NO scripts in the .swu (LUA/SCRIPTS/SHELLHANDLER
  compiled out — pure-data payload, smaller binary, liblua dropped);
  hardware-compatibility against `/etc/hwrevision` is LIVE (bench 2026-09-28):
  the file MUST be two tokens `<boardname> <revision>` (`hw-compatibility.c`
  `fscanf("%ms %ms")`, needs ret==2; the list matches the SECOND token only) —
  a lone `1.0` failed every install with "SW not compatible with hardware";
  we ship `solar-ctl 1.0`. The per-slot kernel image entry MUST be
  `type = "rawfile"` + `path = ...` (FILE_HANDLER, legal in `images:` —
  core/parser.c resolves IMAGE|FILE): `raw` open()s `device=` O_RDWR without
  O_CREAT → "Error streaming uImage" installing into an empty slot dir
  (bench 2026-09-28). Recipe facts: NOT an image recipe — `inherit
  swupdate-common solar-swu-signing image-artifact-names` (without the last,
  IMAGE_NAME/IMAGE_LINK_NAME are unset → dashed filenames), `S = "${UNPACKDIR}"`
  comes from the class, full entry names in `SWUPDATE_IMAGES` are matched
  EXACTLY in DEPLOY_DIR_IMAGE (use stable symlinks), `IMAGE_DEPENDS =
  `IMAGE_DEPENDS = "solar-ctl-image"`, squashfs payload via `IMAGE_FSTYPES += "squashfs-xz"`.
  **`RM_WORK_EXCLUDE:append = " ${PN}"` is required in this recipe** (hit
  2026-09-28): `do_swuimage` is sstate-registered by `swupdate-common` but its
  sstate restore does not bring back UNPACKDIR's `sw-description` or
  `swu-signing/*.pem`; plain `rm_work` deletes the workdir, so the next
  no-change build re-ran `do_swuimage` against an empty `${S}`
  (`FileNotFoundError` in `swupdate_expand_bitbake_variables`, and its
  `sstate_task_prefunc` had already deleted the deployed `.swu`). Workdir is
  a few KB. Recovery after the bug bit: `bitbake solar-ctl-swu -c cleansstate`
  (the promoted setscene unpack stamp must die before unpack re-runs).
  **Artifact name has a `.rootfs` infix**: `solar-ctl-swu-raspberrypi0-wifi.rootfs.swu`.
- **sw-description gotchas** (verified by building it): libconfig comments
  must be `/* */`; the `$fn(...)`/`@@VAR@@` expansion regex scans **every
  line including comments** — mentioning `$swupdate_get_sha256(...)` in a
  comment makes do_swuimage try to hash a file named `...`. **`sha256` /
  `installed-directly` are DIRECT image-entry attributes** in 2026.05.1
  (`parser/parser.c` `parse_common_attributes`); inside `properties{}` they are
  an opaque handler-only string dict and the install dies at runtime with
  "Hash not set for ..." (bench 2026-09-28 — an earlier grep of `sha256 =`
  matched both layouts and gave a false pass). Values expand at build time
  from files staged in WORKDIR by the class itself. `do_swuimage` also replayed
  STALE sstate on sw-description edits (bare `addtask swuimage before do_build`
  has no hash link to this recipe's own unpack — "task Succeeded" while
  deploying the old artifact); fixed via
  `do_swuimage[depends] += "${PN}:do_unpack"`.
- **Kernel/dtb off p1** (user decision 2026-09-28): per-slot kernels are
  regular files on ext4 `/data`; boot.scr does `ext4load mmc 0:4
  ${kernel_addr_r} /cores/slot-${slot}/uImage` (p**4**! not 0:3), falls back
  to the top-level FAT uImage (factory card before the seed runs).
  `solar-cores-seed.service` (solar-swu-agent) copies /boot/uImage →
  slot-a on first boot. U-Boot needs `CONFIG_CMD_EXT4`/`CONFIG_FS_EXT4` via
  `fw/recipes-bsp/u-boot/u-boot_%.bbappend` + files/solar-ctl.cfg
  (`u-boot-configure.inc` merges every SRC_URI `*.cfg`). **NO dtb in the
  .swu**: boot uses the p1 DTB+overlays loaded by start.elf (never OTA'd) →
  kernels shipped by OTA must stay compatible with the installed dtb.
- **U-Boot env = raw redundant pair in a hidden SD area, NOT the p1 FAT
  file** (user decision + impl 2026-10-05: every slot switch used to mutate
  FAT metadata — the one structure we promised p1 to be free of; msdos has
  no 5th primary slot, so the 32 KiB region is a wic `--no-table --offset`
  partition, `rawcopy` from DEPLOY_DIR_IMAGE; p2/p3/p4 keep their indexes,
  slot-a lands at 108 MiB (p1 = 4..104 exactly). **The wks p1 must be
  `--fixed-size`, never plain `--size`** (hit 2026-10-05: wic's default
  `overhead_factor=1.3` multiplies non-fixed parts during content sizing —
  `--size 100` silently became 130 MiB, walked over the hidden area's
  `--offset`, and do_image_wic died with "Could not place mmcblk02 at
  offset 109051904"; the bench-validated 2026-09 images actually had
  slot-a at 136 MiB, unnoticed because every consumer addresses slots by
  index). All geometry
  constants live in `fw/classes/solar-ablayout.bbclass` (boot size → env
  offset derivation, shared by wks.in template, u-boot fragment, fw_env.
  config, blob recipe). U-Boot: `# CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT is not set` +
  `ENV_IS_IN_MMC` + `ENV_REDUNDANT` + both `CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET(_REDUND)`
  hex symbols are ALL generated from the class constants at configure time
  — `do_configure:prepend` writes `${B}/solar-env-redundant.cfg` (SRC_URI
  cfg files are verbatim, bitbake never expands file contents),
  `do_configure:append` post-merges it (`merge_config.sh -m -O`) +
  **`olddefconfig`** + greps that bbfatal on silently-dropped symbols.
  **Never enable the MMC env backend in a SRC_URI `*.cfg` and never use
  `oldconfig` here** (hit 2026-10-05: `u-boot-configure.inc` runs
  `cml1_do_configure = yes '' | oe_runmake oldconfig` over SRC_URI cfgs
  BEFORE any bbappend `:append` body; `ENV_IS_IN_MMC` without values makes
  the defaultless hex `ENV_OFFSET` prompt, empty `yes` answers re-prompt
  forever — an infinite loop that wrote a 60 GB log.do_configure before
  exit 137; olddefconfig is promptless and cannot hang). Byte layout
  VERIFIED against both
  sides of the wire: per copy `[crc32 LE over DATA ONLY][flags u8][data
  ENV_SIZE-5]` (u-boot env_internal.h ENV_HEADER_SIZE=4+1, libubootenv
  uboot_env_redund — identical); higher flags wins, seed = copy0 flag0 +
  copy1 flag1 so first saveenv heals copy0. Blob bytes + merged `.config`
  asserts PASSED in build 2026-10-05 (`ENV_OFFSET=0x6800000`,
  `ENV_OFFSET_REDUND=0x6804000`, `# CONFIG_ENV_MMC_USE_DT is not set`,
  FAT sub-symbols gone, 32768-B blob CRCs/flags verified). `/etc/fw_env.config` (legacy
  2-line redundant form) is rewritten by a **`do_install[postfuncs]`**
  python in the u-boot bbappend: postfuncs run after ALL do_install bodies
  including other layers' `:append` — a second `do_install:append` would
  LOSE to meta-raspberrypi's (its prio 9 parses after our 6, FILESEXTRAPATHS
  first-match likewise favors them); ownership stays in ${PN}-env. libubootenv
  docs confirm: 2 entries = redundant pair; file paths AND raw block devices
  both legal; negative offsets = from end of device.
- **The env blob must be shipped, pre-built, complete** (bench
  2026-09-25). `fw/recipes-bsp/u-boot/solar-uboot-env_0.1.bb` deploys
  `uboot-env-redundant.bin` = 2 × 16384 bytes, each 4-byte LE CRC32 +
  flags + **full u-boot default env + `slot=a\0`** + NUL pad
  (zlib.crc32 over the data bytes only). **slot-only blobs are a
  trap** (hit 2026-09-28 first bench boot of the factory image): U-Boot treats
  a valid-CRC env as COMPLETE, so bootcmd/bootdelay vanish — autoboot and even
  `boot` become silent no-ops; recovery is `env default -a` + `env save` from
  the U-Boot prompt. The recipe therefore merges the deploy artifact
  `u-boot-initial-env-<machine>-<pv>` (u-boot.inc deploys it as KEY=VALUE
  text; `do_deploy[depends] += "virtual/bootloader:do_deploy"` is ORDERING
  only — bitbake can't hash that file, so touch the recipe after a u-boot
  bump; `do_deploy[vardeps]` pins the class-read SOLAR_UBOOT_* vars — the
  by-name getVar stale-task trap again). libubootenv acceptance of the blob
  format VERIFIED on bench 2026-09-28 (`fw_printenv slot` → `slot=a`, old
  single-copy format). Needs `inherit deploy` (that
  class owns DEPLOYDIR; setting `do_deploy[dirs]="${DEPLOYDIR}"` by hand trips
  the WORKDIR-pollution guard). Lands on the card via the wks hidden rawcopy
  part (was `IMAGE_BOOT_FILES` `uboot.env` until 2026-10-05) + `DEPENDS +=
  solar-uboot-env`. **Bench VERIFIED 2026-10-05** (raw redundant pair, fresh
  image): `fw_printenv slot` → a from the hidden area; manual `fw_setenv
  slot b` + reboot → `root=/dev/mmcblk0p3` with ZERO p1 writes (FAT fallback
  uImage loaded — slot-b had no kernel yet, which also validated that
  path); two full URL OTAs (`solar-update -d "-u http://…"`) B→A and A→B —
  slot-a and slot-b both later booted via ext4load of
  /data/cores/slot-*/uImage; final manual b→a flip back to p2. bootenv
  write via the U-Boot backend + libubootenv into the raw area = live.
  STILL PENDING: the power-cut-mid-fw_setenv test — arm with
  `fw_setenv slot b & sleep 0.01; yank power`, reboot, expect boot anyway
  (higher-flags valid copy wins) and `fw_printenv slot` reporting one
  consistent value.
- **Nothing mounts `/boot` automatically** (bench 2026-09-28): the wrynose
  direct imager writes NO fstab line for the wks `/boot` mountpoint (stock OE
  fstab ships). Since 2026-10-05 the ONLY consumer is `solar-cores-seed`'
  first-boot copy of /boot/uImage (env/slot switches moved to the raw area —
  `fw_setenv` needs no mount now). Fix = `boot.mount` unit in
  solar-swu-agent (`What=/dev/disk/by-label/boot`, vfat, `ro`; enabled via
  `SYSTEMD_SERVICE`). A recipe must NOT `install -d ${D}/boot` (installed-vs-shipped
  QA; the dir already exists in the base rootfs). Overlay trap while
  debugging: writing a file directly into the /etc overlay UPPER
  (`/data/overlay-etc/upper/...`) does not appear through the mounted /etc
  (cached dentry) — write THROUGH /etc instead.
- **Journal persists on /data** (bench-verified 2026-09-28): `/var/log` is a
  symlink to `/data/log` (image postprocess `solar_ab_persist_var_log`), the
  preinit `mkdir -p /data/log` before PID 1, and solar-swu-agent ships
  `/etc/systemd/journald.conf.d/10-solar-ctl.conf` (`Storage=persistent`,
  `SystemMaxUse=32M` + `SystemMaxFileSize=8M` — the caps are the SD-wear
  bound; lower them for long-term production). Keeps the journal off the
  512 MB tmpfs and alive across reboots: after an OTA flip,
  `journalctl -b -1 -u solar-swupdate-progress` shows the *previous* boot's
  update (bench: boots -1/0 listed). Preinit-failure note: if /data never
  mounts, the link is dangling and journald falls back to /run.
- **/data (p4) self-heal in the overlayfs-etc preinit**: image ships its own
  `OVERLAYFS_ETC_INIT_TEMPLATE` (`files/solar-overlayfs-etc-preinit.sh.in`):
  mount → e2fsck -y → mkfs.ext4 -F last resort; boot never blocks. **Trap:**
  the class renders the template with python `str.format()` — any literal
  `{`/`}` (even in comments, and shell-function braces) breaks do_rootfs;
  the upstream template is brace-free for exactly this reason.
- **SWUpdate update state was a trap with `BOOTLOADER_NONE`** (void for our
  config 2026-09-28: U-Boot backend is selected now, so those calls persist —
  kept as knowledge, NONE is still compiled in): the "Update Status
  Storage" choice has exactly ONE option (`UPDATE_STATE_CHOICE_BOOTLOADER`,
  which `depends on ... || BOOTLOADER_NONE || ...`), so it is force-enabled and
  there is no file-based option to pick. `bootloader/none.c` implements the env
  on a `static struct dict` = **RAM only, returns success, gone at reboot**. So
  `ustate`/`swupdate-env`/`bootstate=`/`set_bootloader_state` silently persist
  nothing → keep all boot-state bookkeeping in `/data` yourself.
  **Escape hatch (verified in swupdate 2026.05.1 sources, no C needed):**
  `CONFIG_BOOTLOADER_GRUB=y` is a *file-backed* env and `GRUBENV_PATH` is a
  **Kconfig string**, not hardcoded — point it at ext4 `/data` and those calls
  really persist. Costs: the file must be **exactly 1024 bytes** with the
  `# GRUB Environment Block\n` header (pre-create it; writes go via
  `grubenv.new`+rename, so same-fs only), and it reports "grub" on a board with
  no GRUB. **Trap:** the `choice "Default Bootloader Interface"` has no `default`
  statement, so making GRUB *visible* silently flips the default off `none`
  (GRUB precedes NONE in the choice) — pin `BOOTLOADER_DEFAULT_NONE` explicitly.
- `overlayfs-etc.bbclass` (oe-core) is the `/etc` mechanism, BUT its default
  `OVERLAYFS_ETC_CREATE_MOUNT_DIRS=1` does `mount -o remount,rw /` — on a
  squashfs root that can never work. Set it to `0` and pre-create `/data`.
  Also conflicts with IMAGE_FEATURES `package-management`.
- `overlayfs.bbclass` (for `/var`) requires the **`overlayfs` DISTRO_FEATURE,
  which is NOT in `DISTRO_FEATURES_DEFAULTS`** in fw/conf/distro/solar-ctl.conf
  — must be added. The kernel side is already there: `CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS=m`,
  `CONFIG_SQUASHFS=m` (+`SQUASHFS_XZ=y`) in `bcmrpi_defconfig` (verified
  2026-09-24 in work-shared, kernel 6.18.33) — the image merely lacks the
  `kernel-module-overlay`/`kernel-module-squashfs` **packages**, not the
  symbols. It refuses `/etc` by design.
  `/var/volatile` for RO rootfs is initscripts-only → systemd never runs it.
- Slot switching: `tryboot` is the mechanism — firmware sets a one-shot flag,
  clears it, and loads `tryboot.txt` **instead of** `config.txt`. Kernel side
  verified (`drivers/firmware/raspberrypi.c` parses `reboot="0 tryboot"` →
  `RPI_FIRMWARE_SET_REBOOT_FLAGS`, binds on bcm2835-firmware). Arm with
  `echo '0 tryboot' > /run/systemd/reboot-param && systemctl reboot` (systemd>=254).
  `autoboot.txt`/`tryboot_a_b` exists but legacy start.elf support is untested.
  Nothing decrements a boot counter (tryboot is consumed pre-kernel) → rely on
  `panic=N` + per-slot `slot=A|B` cmdline token, not a bootcount.
- meta-swupdate has a `wrynose` branch; layer is at the **repo root** (kas entry
  needs no `layers:` key), `LAYERDEPENDS_swupdate = "openembedded-layer"` (we
  carry meta-oe). Recipes: `swupdate.inc` + `swupdate_2025.12/2026.05.1/git.bb`
  sharing one `swupdate/defconfig`; default provider = 2026.05.1. Configured by
  **its own Kconfig**, no PACKAGECONFIG: `swupdate.inc` inherits `cml1`, so
  **any `*.cfg` in SRC_URI is a config fragment** — do_configure concatenates
  flags + `defconfig` + `find_cfgs()` (every SRC_URI `*.cfg`) then
  `merge_config.sh -m` (last wins) + `olddefconfig`. Ours:
  `fw/recipes-support/swupdate/swupdate/solar-ctl.cfg`.
  DEPENDS are computed by an anon python in `swupdate.inc` over the **text of
  defconfig overlaid with every SRC_URI `*.cfg`** (regex
  `^(?:# )?(CONFIG_*)[= ]`), not the merged `.config` — so `CONFIG_DOWNLOAD=y`
  in our fragment really adds `curl` (mapping: `DOWNLOAD`|`SURICATTA`→curl,
  `UBOOT`→libubootenv DEPENDS **+ RDEPENDS**, `SSL_IMPL_OPENSSL`→openssl...).
  **Parse-cache trap (hit 2026-09-28):** that python reads the fragment files
  directly, outside bitbake's parse-cache file tracking — editing
  `solar-ctl.cfg` on a warm cache yields a STALE parse (old DEPENDS) plus the
  "metadata is not deterministic" basehash errors, and the task then runs with
  an old sysroot (symptom: `channel_curl.c: fatal error: curl/curl.h` while
  `bitbake -e swupdate` *now* shows curl in DEPENDS). Fix: `rm -rf build/cache`
  (full re-parse; sstate untouched) before the next build after a fragment
  edit — warm runs can otherwise replay the stale basehash (the same
  X→Y `not deterministic` error recurs across several warm builds until one
  cold run settles the cache; CI is immune, its `build/cache` is always cold).
  And the fragment regex
  accepts `# CONFIG_FOO is not set`, so that form really removes a base `y` and
  its DEPENDS. Trap: `HAVE_*` are `option env=` symbols probed from the sysroot
  by SWUpdate's own Makefile, so **olddefconfig silently drops** any symbol with
  an unmet `depends on HAVE_*` — never trust "the fragment was applied", read
  the merged `.config` (CI dumps it). `CURL`/`CURL_SSL` are **hidden** (only via
  `SURICATTA`/`DOWNLOAD*`). `libubootenv`/`libconfig`/`json-c` are unconditional
  DEPENDS. Shipped defconfig is wrong for us: `SURICATTA`/`CURL`/
  `SIGNED_IMAGES`/`HASH_VERIFY` all off (note: `CONFIG_UBOOT=y` — the shipped
  `y` was right for us ALL ALONG only since 2026-09-28; we previously turned it
  off because swupdate must not touch the env while fw_setenv owned it — now
  swupdate IS the env writer, see the single-.swu bullet). Hawkbit =
  just `CONFIG_SURICATTA=y` (+CURL_SSL) — a config, not a protocol to implement.
  No RPi bootloader handler exists (`none/ebg/uboot/grub/cboot` only; and
  `BOOTLOADER_NONE` is `default y`) → `bootloader_transaction_marker=false;
  bootloader_state_marker=false;` stay (as per-set properties — default true
  would add p1 FAT writes per install) but the switch is done by the `bootenv`
  section via the U-Boot backend; no `dual_copy` property — standby slot is
  our job.
  **Choice trap (verified 2026-09-28, bootloader/Kconfig):** the `choice
  "Default Bootloader Interface"` has no `default` statement and UBOOT precedes
  NONE — `CONFIG_UBOOT=y` alone silently flips the default; pin
  `CONFIG_BOOTLOADER_DEFAULT_UBOOT=y`. **Handler trap (bench 2026-09-28, first
  solar-update run):** the `bootenv`/`uboot` IMAGE HANDLERS the parser resolves
  are a SEPARATE switch — `CONFIG_BOOTLOADERHANDLER=y` (handlers/boot_handler.c,
  default n); with only the backend built, every install dies in the parser:
  "bootloader support absent but sw-description has bootloader section!". CI
  asserts both. Related edge: if the on-disk env cannot
  be opened, `uboot.c` loads `UBOOT_DEFAULTENV` (/etc/u-boot-initial-env) and a
  later `env_store()` OVERWRITES uboot.env with it; that file is deliberately
  absent from our image so this path errors instead (libubootenv0 +
  libubootenv-bin + u-boot-env/fw_env.config already ship — needed anyway).
  `installed-directly=true` is **mandatory on 512 MB** (else it extracts to
  tmpfs /tmp). `swupdate-www/-client/-ipc/-lua/-progress/-tools/-usb` are
  packages of `swupdate`. The layer also ships **bbclasses** —
  `swupdate-image.bbclass` (`.swu` straight from an image recipe +
  `file://sw-description`) on `swupdate-common.bbclass` (`do_swuimage`,
  `SWUPDATE_IMAGES*`, `SWUPDATE_SIGNING` ⇒ `cpio-native`/`openssl-native`,
  `S = "${UNPACKDIR}"`, signs with `openssl dgst -sha256 -sign`, requires
  `SWUPDATE_PRIVATE_KEY` to EXIST at task time) — this IS the route used
  since 2026-09-28 (via solar-ctl-swu.bb; swupdate-image.bbclass itself is
  NOT inherited — it injects its own image).
- **`wic` moved OUT of oe-core** (verified 2026-09-23: no `scripts/lib/wic`
  on wrynose or master). It is a standalone project consumed as a recipe:
  `meta/recipes-support/wic/wic_0.3.1.bb` → `git://git.yoctoproject.org/wic.git`
  tag v0.3.1, built as `wic-native`. Consequences: canned wks now live in
  **`<layer>/files/wic/`** (so ours goes in `fw/files/wic/`); `image_types_wic`
  gained an `IMAGER=direct` abstraction; plugin source (rawcopy) is only
  greppable locally in `build/downloads/git2/git.yoctoproject.org.wic.git`
  (real path **`src/wic/plugins/source/rawcopy.py`**, not `lib/wic/…`).
  `bitbake wic-native -c fetch` **PASSED 2026-09-24** — smart-HTTPS git works
  even though Cloudflare still 403s the cgit **web** UI; if it ever fails to
  fetch, mirror wic.git to GitHub and override SRC_URI in a bbappend.
- Hazards: `/etc` overlay upper is **shared by both slots and survives
  rollback** (factory reset = wipe the upper dir; app config belongs in
  `/data`); **never OTA `bootcode.bin`/`start.elf`** (corrupt GPU firmware =
  truck roll); keep p1 FAT writes rare; MSDOS table + ext4 **fs labels**
  (`/dev/disk/by-label/`), since `by-partlabel` needs GPT.
- Bootloader version check: `bitbake -e rpi-bootfiles | grep -E
  '^(PV|SRCREV|RPIFW_DATE)='` (PV=`${RPIFW_DATE}`), or the
  `rpi-bootfiles-<PV>.stamp` in the deploy dir; `vcgencmd version` needs
  libraspberrypi-bin (not installed). Bench probe: `fw/tools/ota-probe.sh`.
- **No runtime firmware updater exists in this stack** (verified 2026-09-24
  against meta-raspberrypi `wrynose`): there is **no `rpi-update` recipe** (no
  matching path, and a layer-scoped code search returns zero hits — the tool
  lives upstream in `Hexxeh/rpi-update`, unpackaged). Boot files come from
  `rpi-bootfiles`, which pins `raspberrypi/firmware` to a SRCREV
  (`RPIFW_DATE ?= "20250801"`) and deploys them at build time; `rpi-eeprom`
  exists but its COMPATIBLE_MACHINE is only raspberrypi4, raspberrypi4-64 and
  raspberrypi5 (a Zero W has no EEPROM). Consequence for A/B: a firmware fix is a
  `rpi-bootfiles` bump + rebuild + **supervised p1 maintenance op on the bench**,
  never an OTA path — p1 is shared by both slots, so no slot switch can carry a
  firmware change, and rewriting `start.elf`/`bootcode.bin` in place is the one
  brick-capable action here (doc §9).
- **An RPi bootloader backend for SWUpdate is feasible but deferred** (doc §6.6):
  `doc/source/bootloader_interface.rst` documents the extension point (4 patch
  points: `bootloader/rpi.c` + a `BOOTLOADER_*` define in `include/bootloader.h`
  + Kconfig entry and a `BOOTLOADER_DEFAULT_*` choice entry + one `obj-` line);
  backends are keyed by **string**, not enum, and `core/bootloader.c` skips
  entries whose `funcs` is NULL. Why not worth it: the interface is a key/value
  env and **the Pi has no such thing** (boot choice = which file the firmware
  reads + a one-shot flag), `env_get` cannot read tryboot back (no getter, only
  `SET_REBOOT_FLAGS`), and per-variable `env_set` means FAT writes on p1. Note
  `bootloader_interface.rst`'s supported list is **stale** (omits `cboot`).
  Revisit trigger: stage-3 `SURICATTA`/Hawkbit boot-state reporting.
- **GRUB is an env store, not a bootloader here** (doc §6.6): `start.elf` on
  BCM2835 cannot load GRUB and `BOOTLOADER_GRUB` does NOT switch slots — it only
  backs the key/value env with a file so the state calls persist. Plan of record
  stays `BOOTLOADER_NONE` + bookkeeping in `/data`.
- **U-Boot is the plan of record for per-slot kernels** (doc §5): wrynose
  `RPI_USE_U_BOOT=1` deploys `u-boot.bin` as `kernel.img` (`rpi_0_w_defconfig`).
  `RPI_USE_U_BOOT=1` + `ENABLE_UART=0` is a hard `bbfatal`; we **keep**
  `ENABLE_UART=1` (already on). UART vs RS485 is hardware: split MAX485 DE
  (GPIO17, pulldown) from /RE (pull-up) so the chip is deaf+mute until Linux;
  production `boot.scr` uses `bootdelay=-2`. Never OTA `u-boot.bin`/`start.elf`.
  Stock `rpi-u-boot-scr` has no A/B — we write `boot.cmd`. Env + `bootcount` live
  on ext4 `/data`, not FAT. Layout: p1 vfat (GPU+U-Boot + `slot-a/`/`slot-b/`
  kernels) + p2/p3 squashfs-xz roots + p4 `/data`. Smoke-verified 2026-09-25:
  U-Boot 2026.01 (musl) boots Linux via the stock `boot.scr` — `bootcmd=
  bootflow scan`, `bootdelay=2`, prompt `U-Boot>`, banner→kernel ~6 s; an
  input byte inside the 2 s window interrupts autoboot (board waits at the
  prompt, not bricked).
- **Bench protocol is doc §8** (tests 0–5, each with commands + what decision it
  flips + a re-evaluation matrix), not a 4-row table any more. Key property:
  `tryboot` is consumed pre-kernel, so a wrong answer **reboots back to
  `config.txt` by itself** — nothing can brick the board, and nothing can be
  verified *before* the reboot (evidence = `/proc/cmdline` + serial log after).
  Fallback if `start.elf` won't vary the cmdline per boot is **not** rewriting
  `cmdline.txt` (every boot needs it → corrupt = truck roll) but a small
  **initramfs** that picks the slot from a marker on `/data` and `switch_root`s
  by ext4 label. `ota-probe.sh` is strictly read-only, busybox-ash safe
  (validated with `busybox sh` + `busybox awk`), and takes `OTA_PROBE_BOOT=<dir>`
  to inspect a card in a bench reader.
- **Bench 2026-09-24 (retested same day; `fw/docs/bench-2026-09-24.md`, firmware
  20250801):** 1a PASS (11 s vs 6 s), 1b FAIL (`cmdline=` ignored), 1c FAIL
  (`kernel=` ignored) → classic Tier 1 dead. Test 2 PASS: `autoboot.txt` is
  parsed; channel is `/chosen/bootloader/partition` (1 unarmed → 9 armed),
  not `partnum`. Bogus p9 self-heals same boot. Tier 2 live but landing on a
  second FAT unproven. Plan of record after 1c + MAX485 isolation: **U-Boot +
  per-slot kernel** (Tier 1-alt remains the no-second-stage fallback). Test 3 PASS (FAT marker
  survives power pull). Test 4 ≈10/21 MB/s. Bugs: no WiFi firmware in image;
  root never resized (135 MB on 122 GB). Serial: CH341 `/dev/ttyUSB0` (FT232R
  dead). Do not OTA `bootcode.bin`/`start.elf`.
- **Bench test 5 PASS (2026-09-25, milestone image `20260925194720`):** U-Boot +
  per-slot kernel A/B layout validated end-to-end — squashfs root on p2, `/etc`
  overlay upper on `/data` (edit survives reboot AND slot switch = §9 hazard
  confirmed), A→B→A flip via `mount -o remount,rw /boot; fw_setenv slot b|a;
  mount -o remount,ro /boot; reboot` (cmdline shows p3/p2 accordingly). Two
  gotchas: (1) **root on squashfs needs `CONFIG_SQUASHFS=y`** —
  bcmrpi_defconfig has `=m` and with no initramfs the kernel panics `VFS:
  Unable to mount root fs on unknown-block(179,2)`; fixed in
  `solar-ctl-slim.cfg` (the `kernel-module-squashfs` package then ceases to
  exist — don't `IMAGE_INSTALL` it); `overlay.ko` staying `=m` is fine (loaded
  from the mounted root). (2) **libubootenv cannot create `/boot/uboot.env`**
  ("Cannot initialize environment") — it must pre-exist at exactly
  `CONFIG_ENV_SIZE` (16 KiB): seed once with `dd` zeros + `fw_setenv -s
  defenv.txt`; step 5 should ship the blob via `IMAGE_BOOT_FILES`. systemd
  self-overlays `/var/{cache,lib,spool}` on tmpfs — works on a RO root, no
  `overlayfs.bbclass` needed.

## C++ style (user preference, 2026-10-06)
- Every `.cpp` (NOT headers) puts `using namespace std;` after its include
  block and uses bare names — no `std::` prefixes — except where an
  unqualified name would genuinely collide. Validated: zero new warnings in
  inv_ctl (glibmm/LVGL/SDL2) and fbdump; C-library names are safe because
  the C++ headers pull the global names into std as the same entity.
- Structs/lists are initialized as far as possible **at construction** —
  `{}`/designated-init/value ctors, not "declare then assign fields one by
  one" (2026-10-06 sweep: fbdump `Sink` got a real ctor, `Geo` from the
  ioctls is one designated aggregate assignment; members that can't be
  constexpr-filled keep NSDMI defaults).
- Read-only strings are `string_view` (params and aliases, both projects,
  2026-10-06). C boundaries that need null termination (wext ioctl, sysfs
  paths, `access`, LVGL `set_file`) get ONE materialized copy at the
  boundary (`char ifn[IFNAMSIZ]{}` / `const string fb{fbdev}`), never
  `sv.data()`-into-C. `sv` has no `c_str()` — fprintf uses `%.*s`.

## inv_ctl app (added 2026-10-01, bench verified 2026-10-02)
- Repo-root `inv_ctl/` is a standalone CMake project; Yocto recipe
  `fw/recipes-apps/inv-ctl/inv-ctl_0.1.bb` (filename = PN = `inv-ctl`, which
  IMAGE_INSTALL + SYSTEMD_SERVICE must match). Backends compile-gated:
  SDL2 (native, FetchContent lvgl pinned to meta-oe's SRCREV) vs
  `lv_linux_fbdev_*` (target); `--backend sdl|fb`, `--fb DEVICE`; the fb
  backend retries forever until /dev/fb0 exists (panel probe + init-fw delay).
- SRC_URI plumbing for the repo-root app dir (validated 2026-10-01): in a
  `.bb`, `${LAYERDIR}` inside FILESEXTRAPATHS stays LITERAL (it is a
  layer.conf variable) and absolute `file://` SRC_URIs path-preserve under
  UNPACKDIR (destsuffix ignored for dirs). Working recipe:
  `FILESEXTRAPATHS:prepend := "${@os.path.abspath('${THISDIR}/../../..')}:"`
  + `SRC_URI = "file://inv_ctl"` + `S = "${UNPACKDIR}/inv_ctl"`.
- `PACKAGECONFIG:pn-lvgl = "fbdev"` in the distro conf (meta-oe default is
  `drm` → wrong driver). Despite `LV_USE_EVDEV` the packaged liblvgl.so
  auto-shlibs to libc/musl only (raw evdev ioctls) — no libevdev runtime
  dep in the image (verified via pkgdata FILERDEPENDS).
- Packaged lvgl ships no pkg-config/cmake files: app CMake finds it via
  `find_path(lvgl.h, PATH_SUFFIXES lvgl)` + `find_library(lvgl)`; the
  -dev tree at /usr/include/lvgl/ carries the Kconfig-expanded lv_conf.h
  next to lvgl.h, auto-detected by `__has_include` in lv_conf_internal.h.
  Native parity build: lv_conf.h overrides via -D defines work (all
  defaults are `#ifndef`-guarded); LVGL 9.4 cmake needs
  CONFIG_LV_BUILD_{DEMOS,EXAMPLES}=OFF cache vars.
- glibmm 2.88 API reality: `Glib::signal_unix_signal` is GONE (use GLib's
  `g_unix_signal_add`); `OptionGroup::add_entry` takes
  `(OptionEntry, Glib::ustring&)` — no string-triple convenience form.
- Display blocker RESOLVED 2026-10-01 and **bench-verified 2026-10-02**: the
  NV3007 init sequence now ships as `/lib/firmware/panel-mipi-dbi-spi.bin`
  (recipe `solar-panel-fw`, fw/recipes-support/solar-panel-fw). Blob is
  generated, never hand-edited, by `fw/tools/lvgl-nv3007-to-mipi-dbi.py`,
  which parses LVGL 9.4's in-tree NV3007 driver
  (`src/drivers/display/nv3007/lv_nv3007.c` — its init list is itself based
  on Arduino_GFX) straight to the kernel firmware-bin format. Re-run the
  tool with `--dump` and review when bumping LVGL. Firmware format
  (authoritative: `drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/panel-mipi-dbi.c`, kernel 6.18.33):
  magic `"MIPI DBI"`+7 NUL, u8 version=1, then `cmd,num_params,params…`;
  a delay is NOP `0x00,0x01,<ms>`. Two gotchas: (1) LVGL delays are in
  **10 ms units** (`lv_lcd_generic_mipi_send_cmd_list`), so the post-SLPOUT
  delay 22 → 220 ms (fits the u8 ms field). (2) The overlay needs
  `write-only;` — the TZT module's 8-pin header has no MISO, and without it
  the driver's `mipi_dbi_display_is_on` read can spuriously return "already
  on" and skip the whole init list. Kernel does HW+soft reset +5 ms before
  running the list; the LVGL list ends in DISPON. **Bench-verified
  2026-10-02:** glass lit, ruler pattern flush at both ends, watch UI
  upright and aligned (IPS panel — no INVON fiddling like the TN ILI9488
  clones needed). Overlay `spi-max-frequency` default is 16 MHz (panel
  spec 32 MHz; bench card ran `dtoverlay=nv3007,speed=2000000` on flying
  leads — pixel noise on glass = too fast, override with `speed=<Hz>`).
  Bring-up narrative (symptom → cause → fix, one entry per trap): **
  `fw/docs/display-nv3007.md`**.
- WiFi power-save: brcmfmac defaults PS **on** → multi-second SSH/KEX
  stalls (mlkem768-size replies; laptop workaround `ssh -o
  KexAlgorithms=curve25519-sha256`). wpa_supplicant 2.11 here REJECTS
  `set_network ps 0` (FAIL — field unsupported; `scan_ssid 1` → OK, so
  the command itself works, the field is unsupported). Kill it with
  `iw dev wlan0 set power_save off` — retry loop in
  solar-wifi.service `ExecStartPost`, `iw` in the recipe RDEPENDS.
- SSH root key: baked by `solar-rootkeys` from `SOLAR_SSH_PUBLIC_KEY`
  (see Firmware build env bullet). Use plain ed25519/RSA pubkeys;
  sk-*/YubiKey pubkeys verify natively but prompt for a touch on EVERY
  connection (the friction that killed them, 2026-10-02).
- inv_ctl signal: /proc/net/wireless prints the iface as `%-8s:` — the
  padding sits BEFORE the colon, so `"%63[^:]:"` captures `wlan0   `
  (padded) and the strcmp silently fails (UI showed `--`); the link
  column can print as "44/70". net.cpp `query_signal` parses token-wise.
  Second trap same column set (fixed 2026-10-02, OTA'd same day): the
  wext **status** token is `0000` for ALL mac80211 drivers (brcmfmac
  included) even when fully associated — legacy ad-hoc-only field — so
  linked must come from `/sys/class/net/<if>/carrier` (`query_carrier`),
  never `atoi(status)` (UI showed "WiFi: no link" while `iw` said
  Connected). Also level prints WITH trailing dot ("-66.") — strtod
  eats it; "99/99"/"--" markers still rejected. Third trap same line
  (fixed + OTA'd 2026-10-02): wext-proc emits `" %-8s:"` — there is a
  LEADING space before the iface name too; trimming only the
  pre-colon padding leaves " wlan0", strcmp never matches and the UI
  query_signal failure zeroing it). Trim BOTH ends.
- inv_ctl unit tests (added 2026-10-02): CTest + Catch2 v3 (amalgamated,
  `EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL`), harness gated by `INV_CTL_BUILD_TESTS` (default OFF
  — the Yocto build never sees Catch2 or a FetchContent at do_configure) and
  `INV_CTL_BUILD_UI=OFF` (skips glibmm/SDL2/LVGL entirely — net.cpp is libc
  + syscalls). Run: `cmake -DINV_CTL_BUILD_UI=OFF -DINV_CTL_BUILD_TESTS=ON`
  + `ctest --test-dir <dir>`. CI: parallel `unit-tests` job in firmware.yml
  (no kas, no secrets). golden /proc/net/wireless inputs = bench captures;
  golden inputs replay via tmpfile(). Catch2 comes from GitHub (v3.7.1,
  EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL needs CMake>=3.28 — runner-pinned ubuntu-24.04 provides
  cmake 3.28; the Yocto build never configures the test branch).
  `parse_wext` is **regex-based by user preference** (readability,
  2026-10-02; the tests are its safety net): the `(?:\s|$)` tail is
  load-bearing — it rejects the "--"/"99/99"/"-67.." markers, and an
  early variant without the optional `\.?` broke the real "-67."
  trailing-dot level. std::regex over a C `char[]` line needs
  **std::cmatch** — `smatch` is `string::const_iterator`-based and
  will not bind (GCC 16 spelled it out; the build failing silently
  left ctest replaying the stale binary as a false 10/10).
- inv_ctl board identity (added 2026-10-06): status panel shows
  `/sys/firmware/devicetree/base/{model,serial-number}` (bench capture:
  each file is ONE NUL-terminated string, no newline — parser also
  tolerates `\n`); gate = model prefix "Raspberry Pi", so a laptop
  (x86, no DT at all) gets an empty `BoardInfo` and the labels are
  never created. Zero W serial prints old-format 16-hex
  `0000000047ec1e46` — the leading zeros are real, don't trim.
  `test_board.cpp` #includes `board.cpp`; its fixture writes NUL bytes
  with explicit length (the net fixture's strlen would truncate).
- LVGL 9.4 antialiasing has **no config knob**: `disp->antialiasing`
  defaults to 1 for `LV_COLOR_DEPTH > 8` (lv_display.c), and
  `lv_display_set_antialiasing()` warns "Disabling anti-aliasing is
  not supported since v9". Text AA is baked into the 4 bpp Montserrat
  glyph bitmaps. Both our builds are depth 32 → AA is on, nothing to
  enable (verified against the pinned SRCREV source, 2026-10-06).
- Bench serial quirks: the default console is the **mini-UART** — it eats
  chars on lines >~60; wake with `\r`, flush with `\025\003`, never type
  3.4 KB base64 lines (wget over LAN instead). CH341 dongle drops off
  USB — re-seat when it vanishes. Never pipe a timeout-bound capture
  through `tail` (buffer lost); redirect to a file. busybox: no
  `head -4`/`head -c` quirks-free — use `head -n 4` / `dd`.
- Bench state (2026-10-02, fresh image flashed): glass lit at the image
  default **16 MHz** with no pixel noise, watch UI upright and aligned;
  sole defect found = fbcon terminal text on the panel (fix in tree:
  FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE off in solar-ctl-slim.cfg — until that kernel is
  built+flashed, the runtime workaround is
  `echo 0 > /sys/class/vtconsole/vtcon1/bind`). /tmp files volatile —
  re-fetch after each reboot.

## Editor on target
- Use **busybox `vi`** — decided 2026-09 after evaluating classic nvi 1.81.6:
  it fails to build on wrynose's GCC (2003-era code calls `conv_init`/`conv_enc`
  with no prototypes anywhere in the tarball; implicit decls are hard errors
  since GCC 14). Don't retry nvi without backporting the missing prototypes
  (plus stale bundled config.sub — needs gnu-config copy). Also needs db
  compat185 bbappend for `dbopen()`. Not worth it for a Zero W image.

## Device facts
- Zero W WiFi/BT chip: BCM43430. `IMAGE_INSTALL` needs **both**
  `linux-firmware-rpidistro-bcm43430` (the machine-conf RRECOMMENDS did not
  land it in the 2026-09-18 image) **and** `kernel-module-brcmfmac-cyw`:
  kernel 6.18 brcmfmac runtime-`request_module()`s the vendor firmware
  plugin per chip (cyw/bca/wcc); the name is built at runtime in
  `fwvid.c`, so modpost records no softdep ⇒ the package is never
  auto-installed; without it `modprobe brcmfmac-cyw` fails and there is no
  `wlan0` (seen 2026-09-25). Driver `brcmfmac`.
- Console: UART 115200 8N1; image has dropbear but **root has no password**
  by default (set via serial `passwd`, or lab-only `empty-root-password`).
- SSH policy: `/etc/default/dropbear` (our `dropbear.default` via the
  bbappend) sets `DROPBEAR_EXTRA_ARGS="-s"` — password logins disabled,
  root key login allowed. **dropbear `-B` means "allow blank password
  logins", NOT "reject passwords"** — never use it for key-only policy
  (with the lab `empty-root-password` feature, older dropbear would then
  accept a blank root password over SSH; 2025.89 happens to reject blank
  passwords anyway, but that is an accident, not the mechanism).
- Image artifact: `build/tmp/deploy/images/raspberrypi0-wifi/*.wic.bz2`;
  flash with `bmaptool copy` to the raw SD device.
